    // Method to add two numbers
    static int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }

    // Method to subtract two numbers
    static int subtract(int a, int b) {
        return a - b;
    }

    // Method that performs an operation using a given operation function
    static int performOperation(int a, int b, Operation operation) {
        return operation.perform(a, b);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = 10;
        int y = 5;

        // Pass a lambda expression as a parameter for addition
        int result1 = Calculator.performOperation(x, y, (a, b) -> a + b);
        System.out.println("Result of addition: " + result1); // Output: 15

        // Pass a lambda expression as a parameter for subtraction
        int result2 = Calculator.performOperation(x, y, (a, b) -> a - b);
        System.out.println("Result of subtraction: " + result2); // Output: 5
    }
}
```

In this updated code:

- We use lambda expressions `(a, b) -> a + b` and `(a, b) -> a - b` to represent the addition and subtraction operations, respectively.
